problem_statement:
[Original Issue]
[Feature Request] TypeScript make generated codes from enum could be minified when not used
## Feature Request

**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**

For now TypeScript will transform enum from

```ts
enum Test {
    Key = 1
}
```
to

```ts
var Test;
(function (Test) {
    Test[Test["Key"] = 1] = "Key";
})(Test || (Test = {}));
```
This result is not friendly for uglyify or tree-shaking.
When `Test` is not be used, the generated code block always remain as dead codes.

**Describe the solution you'd like**

prefer to generate codes below:
```ts
var Test = /*#__PURE__*/(function () {
    var e = {}
    e[e["Key"] = 1] = "Key";
    return e
})();
```
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1667873/46602882-0d778d00-cb24-11e8-8847-cbb3483e0960.png)

The suggestion version will be removed.

related: https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/issues/27604
custom plugin: https://github.com/morlay/babel-plugin-typescript-iife-enum

[Multimodal Context - Compact]
[Visual Evidence] Image 1: https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1667873/46602882-0d778d00-cb24-11e8-8847-cbb3483e0960.png **Raw Visual Description** UI shows UglifyJS 3 minifier with two code panes: left (input) and right (minified output). Input contains TypeScript enum code with `var Test; (function (Test) { ... })` pattern. Minified output is 76 bytes, 63.46% smaller, but retains the same structure — no `/*#__PURE__*/` annotation or dead code removal. **Issue-Relevant Analysis** TypeScript’s enum transpilation generates IIFE code that UglifyJS cannot tree-shake because it lacks `/*#__PURE__*/` markers. The requested fix is to emit `/*#__PURE__*/`-annotated IIFE code (e.g., `var Test = /*#__PURE__*/(function () { ... })();`) so unused enums can be removed during minification. **Localization Clues** - UI element: “UglifyJS 3: Online JavaScript minifier” header. - Text: “The minified output (76 bytes, saved 63.46%)” — indicates minification success but not dead code removal. - Code pattern: `var Test; (function (Test) { ... })` — the problematic output format. - Suggested fix: `/*#__PURE__*/` annotation — key clue for localization. [Web Evidence] URL 1: https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/issues/27604 Summary: [Feature] make generated codes from enum could be minified when not used · Issue #27604 · microsoft/TypeScript · GitHub Search Terms For now TypeScript will transform enum from enum Test { Key = 1 } to var Test; (function (Test) { Test[Test["Key"] = 1] = "Key"; })(Test || (Test = {})); This result is not friendly for uglyify or tree-shaking. When Test is ... [Feature] make generated codes from enum could be minified when not used · Issue #27604 · microsoft/TypeScript · GitHub Skip to content Navigation Menu Toggle navigation Sign in Appearance settings Platform AI CODE CREATION GitHub Copilot Write better code with AI GitHub Copilot app Direct agents from issue to merge MCP Registry New I... URL 2: https://github.com/morlay/babel-plugin-typescript-iife-enum Summary: GitHub - morlay/babel-plugin-typescript-iife-enum · GitHub Contribute to morlay/babel-plugin-typescript-iife-enum development by creating an account on GitHub. GitHub - morlay/babel-plugin-typescript-iife-enum · GitHub Skip to content Navigation Menu Toggle navigation Sign in Appearance settings Platform AI CODE CREATION GitHub Copilot Write better code with AI GitHub Copilot app Direct agents from issue to merge MCP Registry New Integrate external tools DEVELOPER WORKFLOWS Ac...

