hints_text:
The intention was to support these often-requested cases:
```js
function test(is) {
  if (is) {
    taskA()
  }
  // case 1 "comment before else"
  else if (!is) {
    taskB()
  } // case 2 "comment after }", for things like "// end if ..."
  else taskC()
}
```
This issue might be an unintended side-effect of fixing that.

